description:
Ask the learner a GRADED question with a known correct answer, then instantly grade and give feedback. Unlike ask_user_question (which collects preferences/decisions with no right answer), probe always has a correct answer supplied by you, marks the learner's selection right/wrong, reveals the correct answer, and can show an explanation. Options-only: single-select or multi-select, plus an automatic 'I don't know' choice so the learner can signal a genuine gap instead of guessing. An always-present optional thinking field lets the learner attach his reasoning to ANY answer; it reaches you only when non-empty. No free-text answers — for non-graded questions use ask_user_question instead. ONE question per turn: call a single probe, then end your turn — his answer determines the next.
Example arguments — copy the escaping exactly: inside JSON strings a LaTeX backslash is \\ and a newline is \n.
```json
{
  "question": "A signal is $y=\\sin(2x)$ and $\\frac{dx}{dt}=3$. What is $\\frac{dy}{dt}$?",
  "options": [
    {
      "label": "$6\\cos(2x)$",
      "value": "a"
    },
    {
      "label": "$2\\cos(2x)$",
      "value": "b"
    },
    {
      "label": "$3\\cos(2x)$",
      "value": "c"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The phase changes twice as fast as $x$; multiply by the sine's slope:\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\cos(2x)\\cdot2\\cdot3=6\\cos(2x)\n$$",
  "correctAnswer": "a"
}
```
